# Naming Knowledge

Names describe purpose. No abbreviations except universal ones (`id`, `url`, `dto`, `otp`, `jwt`).
Follow the closest existing module over this file when they differ.

## Files and folders

kebab-case, with the Nest role suffix. Module folders are plural domain nouns.

| Thing | File | Class / export |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Module | `users.module.ts` | `UsersModule` |
| Controller | `users.controller.ts` | `UsersController` |
| Service | `users.service.ts` | `UsersService` |
| Repository | `users.repository.ts` | `UsersRepository` |
| Mapper | `users.mapper.ts` | `toUserResponse()` (functions) |
| Domain types | `users.types.ts` | `User`, `UserStatus` |
| DTO | `dto/create-user.dto.ts` | `createUserSchema`, `CreateUserDto`, `CreateUserInput` |
| TypeORM entity | `user.entity.ts` | `UserEntity` |
| Guard | `jwt-auth.guard.ts` | `JwtAuthGuard` |
| Decorator | `current-user.decorator.ts` | `CurrentUser` |
| Interceptor / filter / pipe | `request-id.interceptor.ts`, `all-exceptions.filter.ts` | `RequestIdInterceptor`, `AllExceptionsFilter` |
| Port / adapter | `storage.port.ts`, `s3-storage.adapter.ts` | `StoragePort`, `S3StorageAdapter` |
| Unit test | `users.service.spec.ts` | — |
| e2e test | `test/users/list-users.e2e-spec.ts` | — |
| Migration | generated name + snake/pascal description | `add_user_status` / `AddUserStatus` |

One exported class per file. Helper functions may share a file with the thing they serve.

## DTOs

| Purpose | Class | Schema const |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Create body | `CreateUserDto` | `createUserSchema` |
| Update body | `UpdateUserDto` | `updateUserSchema` |
| Action body | `PublishAssignmentDto` | `publishAssignmentSchema` |
| List query | `ListUsersQueryDto` | `listUsersQuerySchema` |
| Path params | `IdParamDto`, `UserSessionParamsDto` | `idParamSchema` |
| Single response | `UserResponseDto` | `userResponseSchema` |
| List response | `UserListResponseDto` | `userListResponseSchema` (= `paginatedSchema(userResponseSchema)`) |

Inferred input types drop `Dto`: `CreateUserInput`, `ListUsersQuery`, `UserResponse`.

## Methods

| Layer | Name | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Repository | `findById`, `findByEmail` | returns `T \| null` |
| Repository | `list(filter, page)` | returns `{ items, nextCursor }` |
| Repository | `create`, `update`, `delete`, `exists…` | plain persistence |
| Service | `getById` | returns `T`, throws `…_NOT_FOUND` |
| Service | `list`, `create`, `update`, `delete` | CRUD use cases |
| Service | verb for actions: `publish`, `archive`, `verifyEmail`, `rotateRefreshToken` | business operations |
| Controller | same name as the service method it calls | — |
| Mapper | `toUser(row)`, `toUserResponse(user)` | pure |

- `find…` may return nothing; `get…` must return or throw. Never mix.
- Booleans: `is…`, `has…`, `can…`, `should…` (`isVerified`, `canPublish`).
- Event handlers / outbox consumers: `on<Event>` (`onUserRegistered`).
- No `handle()`, `process()`, `doStuff()`, `data`, `info`, `manager` as names.

## Types and constants

- Types, interfaces, classes, enums: PascalCase, no `I` prefix, no `Interface`/`Type` suffix.
- Global constants and value tuples: UPPER_SNAKE (`USER_STATUSES`, `MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES`).
- Metadata keys: UPPER_SNAKE (`IS_PUBLIC_KEY`, `ROLES_KEY`).
- Injection tokens for non-class providers: UPPER_SNAKE symbols (`MAIL_TRANSPORT`).

## Database

| Object | Convention | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Table | snake_case, plural | `users`, `challenges`, `transformations` |
| Join table | both plural names, alphabetical | `roles_users` or a named concept `memberships` |
| Column | snake_case | `password_hash`, `company_id` |
| Primary key | `id` (uuid) | — |
| Foreign key column | `<singular>_id` | `user_id` |
| Timestamps | `created_at`, `updated_at`, `<event>_at` | `verified_at`, `deleted_at` |
| Booleans | `is_…` / `has_…` | `is_primary` |
| Unique constraint | `<table>_<cols>_key` | `users_email_key` |
| Index | `<table>_<cols>_idx` | `users_company_id_idx` |
| Foreign key | `<table>_<col>_fkey` | `users_company_id_fkey` |
| Enum type | snake_case singular | `user_status` |
| Enum values | lower_snake | `pending_verification` |

These match Postgres/Prisma defaults, so constraint names are predictable in the error filter.

## API

- Paths: plural kebab-case nouns (`/api/saved-searches`), actions as sub-resource verbs
  (`/api/assignments/{id}/publish`) — `05-api-design`.
- JSON fields camelCase; query params camelCase; enum values lower_snake.
- Headers: `X-CSRF-Token`, `X-Locale`, `X-Request-Id`.
- Cookies: snake_case (`access_token`, `refresh_token`, `csrf_token`).

## Error codes

UPPER_SNAKE, `<DOMAIN>_<CONDITION>`, key equals value in `ErrorCode`:
`USER_NOT_FOUND`, `USER_EMAIL_TAKEN`, `AUTH_OTP_LOCKED`, `FILE_TOO_LARGE`. Generic codes without a
prefix are reserved: `VALIDATION_FAILED`, `RATE_LIMITED`, `CONFLICT`, `INTERNAL_ERROR`,
`CSRF_INVALID`. Validation issue codes and i18n keys are lower_snake.

## Environment variables

UPPER_SNAKE, prefixed by config group: `APP_`, `AUTH_`, `DATABASE_URL`, `MAIL_`/`SMTP_`,
`STORAGE_`/`S3_`, `LOG_`. Units in the name: `AUTH_ACCESS_TTL_SECONDS`, `MAIL_TIMEOUT_MS`,
`STORAGE_MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES`.

## Git

- Branch: `<type>/<TASK-ID>_<short_description>` — `feat/FC-2_password_reset`.
- Commit: `<type>: <description>`, one line, max 70 chars — `16-git`.
